-- title:
--   Universal Drinfeld basis generates the maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $W_0$ a complete discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, equipped with a surjective ring map $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ for which $(0,0)$ is a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ relative to the zero ideal, i.e. `F₀.nthSeries q` is a unit multiple of `F₀.drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`. Let $R$ be a noetherian local $W_0$-algebra, complete for the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic topology, with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ of kernel $\mathfrak m_R$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$ over $W_0$; let $F$ be a commutative formal group law over $R$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_R$ is $F_0$, and let $x_0, x_1 \in \mathfrak m_R$ satisfy the analogous Drinfeld-basis identity `F.nthSeries q = u * F.drinfeldDivisor q x₀ x₁` with $u$ a unit, for the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic topology. Assume the universality hypothesis: for every Artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ of kernel $\mathfrak m_T$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, every commutative law $G$ over $T$ reducing to $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, and all $y_0, y_1 \in \mathfrak m_T$ forming a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for $G$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : R \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_R$ for which there exist a law $F'$ over $T$ obtained from $F$ by base change along $\varphi$ and an isomorphism of laws $\psi : F' \to G$ (a power series with vanishing constant term, unit linear coefficient, and $\psi(F'(X,Y)) = G(\psi(X),\psi(Y))$) whose coefficients reduce to those of $X$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T$ and which carries $\varphi(x_0), \varphi(x_1)$, evaluated $\mathfrak m_T$-adically, to $y_0, y_1$. Then $\mathfrak m_R = (x_0, x_1)$.
--
--   This is the statement that the two members of the universal Drinfeld basis of level $q$ form a generating set, hence a system of parameters, for the maximal ideal of the deformation ring pro-representing height-two commutative formal group laws with a level-$q$ Drinfeld basis. It is the step feeding the conclusion that such a deformation ring is regular of Krull dimension two, and through that the reducedness statements for adic completions of quotients on modular curves with full level structure.
